      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Missing Flash Boundary Checks** In `bootrom.cc`, functions like `ReadFlash`, `EraseFlash`, and `WriteFlash` compute the target address:\n\n```c\nuint32_t addr \u003d EgisBootrom::kFlashBaseAddr + offset;\n\n```\n\nThere are no safeguards ensuring that `offset + length` does not exceed `EgisBootrom::kFlashTotalSize`.\n\n* **Suggestion:** Add a bounds check in these methods before sending the command over USB to prevent commanding the bootrom to access invalid memory regions.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 393,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 394,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "6d644044c87bf5377358117e0ba7ceb2ddc3c5d5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
